{
  "sn5.10:0.1": "Linked Discourses 5.10 ",
  "sn5.10:0.2": "1. Nuns ",
  "sn5.10:0.3": "With Vajirā ",
  "sn5.10:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn5.10:1.2": "Then the nun Vajirā robed up in the morning and, taking her bowl and robe, entered Sāvatthī for alms. ",
  "sn5.10:1.3": "She wandered for alms in Sāvatthī. After the meal, on her return from almsround, she went to the Dark Forest for the day’s meditation, ",
  "sn5.10:1.4": "plunged deep into it, and sat at the root of a tree to meditate. ",
  "sn5.10:1.5": "Then Māra the Wicked, wanting to make the nun Vajirā feel fear, terror, and goosebumps, wanting to make her fall away from immersion, went up to her and addressed her in verse: ",
  "sn5.10:2.1": "“Who created this sentient being? ",
  "sn5.10:2.2": "Where is its maker? ",
  "sn5.10:2.3": "Where has the being arisen? ",
  "sn5.10:2.4": "And where does it cease?” ",
  "sn5.10:3.1": "Then the nun Vajirā thought, ",
  "sn5.10:3.2": "“Who’s speaking this verse, a human or a non-human?” ",
  "sn5.10:3.3": "Then she thought, ",
  "sn5.10:3.4": "“This is Māra the Wicked, wanting to make me feel fear, terror, and goosebumps, wanting to make me fall away from immersion!” ",
  "sn5.10:3.5": "Then Vajirā, knowing that this was Māra the Wicked, replied to him in verse: ",
  "sn5.10:4.1": "“Why do you believe there’s such a thing as a <j>‘sentient being’? ",
  "sn5.10:4.2": "Māra, is this your theory? ",
  "sn5.10:4.3": "This is just a pile of conditions, ",
  "sn5.10:4.4": "you